-- title:
--   The cone gap shifts linearly along the axis
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a real inner product space, let $v \in E$ be a unit vector, $\lVert v \rVert = 1$, and let $\vartheta \in \mathbb{R}$. For $p \in E$ let
--   $$\mathrm{gap}(v,\vartheta,p) = \langle v, p\rangle \sin\vartheta - \lVert p - \langle v,p\rangle v\rVert \cos\vartheta$$
--   be the signed distance from $p$ to the boundary of the half-cone with axis $v$ and apex angle $\vartheta$. Then for every $q \in E$ and every $a \in \mathbb{R}$,
--
--   $$\mathrm{gap}(v,\vartheta,\, q + a v) \;=\; \mathrm{gap}(v,\vartheta,\, q) \;+\; a \sin\vartheta .$$
--
--   The reason is that translating along the axis changes only the component of the point along $v$, leaving the transverse component untouched. This makes the gap an affine function of the axial coordinate, which is what allows the constructions of Sections 4 and 5 to buy a prescribed amount of room inside a cone by moving a controlled distance along the axis.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The scalar $a$ is an arbitrary real (it may be negative, in which case the gap decreases), and $\vartheta$ is an arbitrary real with no restriction to $(0,\pi/2]$. Only the unit-length hypothesis on $v$ is used.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/dbenbenn/quadratic-forms-sobolev/blob/7a1a680db2124d46ce370c91fd450aa454edf491/QuadraticFormsSobolev/ConeGap.lean#L137-L148

